course: dictionary
lesson: 3026
title: Words that show how
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Eagerly» is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, and many adverbs end in -ly.
explain: «The Mole climbed in eagerly; the Rat only snorted and stayed outside.» The Mole is keen and excited, while the Rat's snorting and staying outside show he is not. The contrast gives you the clue.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Toad eagerly scrambled up into the cab of the engine» still works with "keenly and excitedly", so you know Toad was thrilled to climb aboard.
fact: «Eagerly» means in a way that shows you really want to do something and are excited about it.
fact: «Eagerly» can also mean keenly and with much interest, as in «We listened eagerly.»
fact: «Eagerly» is an adverb: it tells you how an action happens.
fact: «Eagerly awaited» means waited for with excitement, and «nodded eagerly» means nodded keenly.
fact: Learning words in common phrases, like «eagerly awaited», helps you remember them.
exercise: «She eagerly opened the present.» What does eagerly tell us? | *She opened it with excitement and a wish to see inside | She opened it slowly and carefully | She opened it by accident | She did not want to open it at all
exercise: «The Mole climbed in eagerly; the Rat only snorted and stayed outside.» Which of the two was keen? | *The Mole | The Rat | Neither of them | Both of them
exercise: «The show was eagerly awaited by everyone.» Find and copy the phrase that means waited for with excitement. | *eagerly awaited | The show | was awaited | by everyone
test: «We listened eagerly to the story.» What does eagerly mean here? | Quietly and sleepily | *Keenly, with much interest | Angrily | Rudely and loudly
test: Toad «eagerly scrambled up into the cab of the engine.» What is the cab? | The ticket office | *The driver's place | The back of the train | The station platform
exam: Jayden says eagerly means slowly. Why is he wrong? | Eagerly means not at all | *Eagerly shows excitement and keen interest, not slowness | Eagerly is a noun for a type of train | Eagerly means slowly and calmly
